cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the analysis artifacts, please cite them as below."
title: "How much of an RNA language model's in-distribution advantage is family exposure? A controlled decomposition on CHANRG"
authors:
  - family-names: Baselizadeh
    given-names: Nima
    email: nimabaselizadeh@gmail.com
    affiliation: Bu-Ali Sina University, Hamedan, Iran
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nimaone/rnalm-family-exposure"
abstract: >-
  Companion code and results for a controlled decomposition of the
  in-distribution advantage of frozen RNA language models (RiNALMo-giga and
  RNA-FM via MultiMolecule) on the CHANRG RNA secondary-structure benchmark:
  no-LM and random-weight-LM controls, per-family training caps,
  size-matched random subsets, a training-scale curve, and family-equal
  weighting.
keywords:
  - RNA secondary structure
  - RNA language models
  - out-of-distribution generalization
  - family exposure
  - benchmarking
  - RiNALMo
  - RNA-FM
  - CHANRG
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
